# Companions (sidequests/companions.js; [companions] and [[adventurer]].hire in design/data/sidequests.toml). Every
# `ttl companion expect` prints "ttl: ..." when it does not hold. Bots do not walk, so nothing here depends on following;
# the party cap uses real FTB parties formed with `ttl as <bot> ftbteams ...` (see party.rcon for why).
# Rules checked: a Life 1 soul cannot hire; the fee must be payable; one companion per soul; online party members plus their
# companions plus the new one may be 5 at most (a party of four with one companion hires nobody more); a companion that
# dies ends the contract; dismiss ends it.
# Expect in the log: "[ttl] companion: TtlBotCompA granted rookie_swordsman for 30 min (<uuid>)", "... contract ended
# (fallen in battle)".
# Also check in game (not asserted): the companion follows its owner (FOLLOW_OWNER) and fights hostile mobs, cannot hurt or
# be hurt by players, comes back after a relog, and boss credit stays with the players (bosses/boss.js counts players only).
ttlbot spawn TtlBotCompA
ttlbot spawn TtlBotCompB
ttlbot spawn TtlBotCompC
ttlbot spawn TtlBotCompD
ttlbot spawn TtlBotCompL
@sleep 2
ttl as TtlBotCompD ftbteams party leave
ttl as TtlBotCompC ftbteams party leave
ttl as TtlBotCompB ftbteams party leave
ttl as TtlBotCompA ftbteams party leave
kubejs stages add TtlBotCompA ttl.life2
kubejs stages add TtlBotCompB ttl.life2
kubejs stages add TtlBotCompC ttl.life2
kubejs stages add TtlBotCompD ttl.life2
kubejs stages remove TtlBotCompL ttl.life2
ttl companion clear TtlBotCompA
ttl companion clear TtlBotCompB
ttl companion clear TtlBotCompC
ttl companion clear TtlBotCompD
clear TtlBotCompA
clear TtlBotCompB
ttl sidequest goto TtlBotCompA tempest_green
ttl sidequest goto TtlBotCompB tempest_green
ttl sidequest goto TtlBotCompL tempest_green
@sleep 3
# Who may hire: Life 1 never; no coins, no companion; 2 gold buys the C-rank knight.
ttl companion expect TtlBotCompL can_hire rookie_swordsman:life
ttl companion expect TtlBotCompB can_hire veteran_knight:fee
give TtlBotCompB tensura:gold_coin 2
ttl companion expect TtlBotCompB can_hire veteran_knight:yes
ttl companion expect TtlBotCompB can_hire apprentice_mage:kind
# A granted companion (test hook: no fee): one per soul.
ttl companion grant TtlBotCompA rookie_swordsman 30
ttl companion expect TtlBotCompA count 1
ttl companion expect TtlBotCompA kind rookie_swordsman
ttl companion expect TtlBotCompA alive yes
ttl companion expect TtlBotCompA can_hire scout:max
# The party cap: A, B, C and D in one party (4) plus A's companion (1) = 5: B may not hire a sixth fighter.
ttl as TtlBotCompA ftbteams party create CompTest
ttl as TtlBotCompA ftbteams party invite TtlBotCompB
ttl as TtlBotCompB ftbteams party join TtlBotCompA
ttl as TtlBotCompA ftbteams party invite TtlBotCompC
ttl as TtlBotCompC ftbteams party join TtlBotCompA
ttl companion expect TtlBotCompB can_hire veteran_knight:yes
ttl as TtlBotCompA ftbteams party invite TtlBotCompD
ttl as TtlBotCompD ftbteams party join TtlBotCompA
ttl companion expect TtlBotCompB can_hire veteran_knight:cap
# A's companion falls: the contract ends, and B may hire again.
execute as TtlBotCompA at @s run kill @e[tag=ttl.comp,distance=..16]
@sleep 1
ttl sidequest poll TtlBotCompA
ttl companion expect TtlBotCompA count 0
ttl companion expect TtlBotCompB can_hire veteran_knight:yes
# The status line and dismiss (the companion dialog's buttons run these as the player). Hiring from a town adventurer
# (`/ttl companion hire`, the "Join my party" button) picks the nearest hireable one; the green's kinds are random, so
# that path is a manual check in game (stand next to a hireable adventurer on the green and press the button).
execute as TtlBotCompB run ttl companion
ttl companion grant TtlBotCompB veteran_knight
ttl companion expect TtlBotCompB kind veteran_knight
execute as TtlBotCompB run ttl companion dismiss
ttl companion expect TtlBotCompB count 0
ttl adventurers clear tempest_green
ttl as TtlBotCompD ftbteams party leave
ttl as TtlBotCompC ftbteams party leave
ttl as TtlBotCompB ftbteams party leave
ttl as TtlBotCompA ftbteams party leave
ttl companion clear TtlBotCompA
ttlbot remove TtlBotCompA
ttlbot remove TtlBotCompB
ttlbot remove TtlBotCompC
ttlbot remove TtlBotCompD
ttlbot remove TtlBotCompL
